00:03:26,666 --> 00:03:32,666
You say you want a revolution?

2
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:59,333
Spice World is a adventure, fantasy, drama film directed by Bob Spiers.

3
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:26,000
World famous pop group the Spice Girls zip around London in their luxurious double
decker tour bus having various adventures and performing for their fans.

4
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:52,666
Victoria - Posh Spice, played by Victoria Beckham.

5
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:19,333
Melanie B - Scary Spice, played by Mel B.

6
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Emma - Baby Spice, played by Emma Bunton.

7
00:24:06,666 --> 00:24:12,666
Melanie C - Sporty Spice, played by Melanie C.

8
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:39,333
Geri - Ginger Spice, played by Geri Halliwell-Horner.

9
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Clifford, played by Richard E. Grant.

10
00:34:26,666 --> 00:34:32,666
Spice World is a 1997 British musical comedy film directed
by Bob Spiers and written by Kim Fuller.

11
00:37:53,333 --> 00:37:59,333
The film stars pop girl group the Spice Girls, who all play themselves.

12
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:26,000
The film — made in a similar vein to the Beatles' 1964 film A Hard Day's Night — depicts a series of fictional events leading up to a major concert at London's Royal Albert Hall, liberally interspersed with dream sequences and flashbacks as
well as surreal moments and humorous asides, whilst also including a subplot dealing with a smear campaign against the Spice Girls by an overzealous newspaper CEO in an attempt to destroy their reputation for his own benefit.

13
00:44:46,666 --> 00:44:52,666
This is the second feature-length film directed by
Spiers, following That Darn Cat (1997).

14
00:48:13,333 --> 00:48:19,333
The film features Richard E.

15
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:46,000
Grant, Alan Cumming, George Wendt, Claire Rushbrook, Mark McKinney and Roger Moore in
supporting roles, with cameo appearances by a number of British celebrities.

16
00:55:06,666 --> 00:55:12,666
Filming took place in London for six of the eight filming weeks and also inside
Twickenham Studios, as well as at over forty famous British landmarks.

17
00:58:33,333 --> 00:58:39,333
Shooting featured several fourteen-hour shooting sessions and a constant,
heavy media presence due to the Spice Girls' popularity.

18
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
The film premiered in the United Kingdom on 15 December 1997, ahead of its wide
theatrical release on the British holiday Boxing Day (26 December).

19
01:05:26,666 --> 01:05:32,666
In North America, it was released on 23 January 1998 by Columbia Pictures.

20
01:08:53,333 --> 01:08:59,333
In the United States, Spice World became a box office success and broke the record for the
highest-ever weekend debut for Super Bowl weekend with box office sales of $10.5 million.

21
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:26,000
The film grossed $56 million at the worldwide box office and received primarily negative reviews
for its lack of cohesive plot, poor acting performances and uninspired humour.

22
01:15:46,666 --> 01:15:52,666
To celebrate its 20th anniversary in 2017, Spice World was given a limited
re-release across the United Kingdom showing at Odeon Cinemas.

23
01:19:13,333 --> 01:19:19,333
Spice World is the highest-grossing film of all time by a musical group.

24
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
It has arguably achieved cult status.

25
01:26:06,666 --> 01:26:12,666
The film explores themes of media, pop star, manager, pop, bus.

26
01:29:33,333 --> 01:29:39,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and mind_bending.
